    "ResetCPU retains a remaining MMIO-clear scheduling discrepancy. The inferred coherent exception-record access view reproduces the complete CPUHostException code and local tables.",
    "WritePhysicalByte and WritePhysicalHalf retain narrow formals. Implicit conversion of ContextRegister DWORD values reproduces the original full-DWORD pushes; explicit casts changed caller code generation.",
    "RunCPU action bits 0x1000 and 0x2000 call SaveState and LoadState(false), respectively, matching the interpreter and original call targets.",
    "RunCPU uses the evidenced local optimization-off setting and symbolic generated-code dispatcher. Its original frame contains32 unreferenced bytes after all used locals and before compiler temporaries. A nested uninitialized byte array models that measured storage; original source-level type, count, name and purpose remain unknown. Changing inferred buffer capacities moved already-correct used-local offsets and was rejected.",
    "RunCPU exact body-plus-table extent is4503bytes; the previous4504 included one alignment byte. Its emitted block to StartCPUThread is4512bytes, including9 CC bytes. StartCPUThread is30bytes followed by2 NOP bytes before0x00416A00.",
    "CPUHostException uses separate 60-byte diagnostic buffers, an explicit valid-index else, and a typed breakpoint assignment loop. The loop naturally emits the observed word copy without the redundant byte tail produced by explicit memcpy. The coherent address-slot view, guarded search snapshot and byte-store local complete the function match.",
    "Relocation target comparisons are performed only when instruction layouts align. ResetCPU leaves 199 target fields not compared; these are separate from unresolved or unverified targets in matching functions.",
    "The earlier unqualified exception-view candidate measured 1782 bytes versus 1802 original bytes; its full-extent comparison and historical hashes are preserved in validation_history. The current coherent view measures and matches all 1802 bytes. ResetCPU remains 1611 bytes versus 1610, with 320 normalized differing bytes.",
